Subject: Re: Variance of the latent variable different than 1 in std.lv
Message-ID: <4Y6gmdKhRj4.3ULI3VthAQAJ@lavaan.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <4Y6gmdKhRj4.6-E0gVSOAAAJ@lavaan.groups.google.com>
References: <4Y6gmdKhRj4.6-E0gVSOAAAJ@lavaan.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/lavaan/c/4Y6gmdKhRj4/m/3ULI3VthAQAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Variances are not model parameters, residual variances are. Residuals variances of exogenous variables are total variances, so the std.lv <http://std.lv> solution coincidentally shows the Habit variance as 1.  The endogenous variables have predictors, so when their total variance == 1, their residual variance == 1 - R^2 < 1.

Terrence D. Jorgensen
Assistant Professor, Methods and Statistics
Research Institute for Child Development and Education, the University of Amsterdam
http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen

