> I was wondering given this answer <https://stats.stackexchange.com/a/258583/140365> by Dr. Cheung, how I can calculate the "Standard Error" of my "New.Effect.Size"?

You can use the delta method, the same way Mike Cheung showed you in that link.  Define your effect size as a parameter in the model syntax, and your summary() output will show your estimated SE for the defined effect size.  You could also use the Monte Carlo method (see the semTools package: ?monteCarloMed help page examples).

Terrence D. Jorgensen
Assistant Professor, Methods and Statistics
Research Institute for Child Development and Education, the University of Amsterdam
http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen

